DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     Checkpoints the current state of _p_o_o_l , which can be later restored by
     zzppooooll iimmppoorrtt ----rreewwiinndd--ttoo--cchheecckkppooiinntt.  The existence of a checkpoint in a
     pool prohibits the following zzppooooll subcommands: rreemmoovvee, aattttaacchh, ddeettaacchh,
     sspplliitt, and rreegguuiidd.  In addition, it may break reservation boundaries if
     the pool lacks free space.  The zzppooooll ssttaattuuss command indicates the exis‐
     tence of a checkpoint or the progress of discarding a checkpoint from a
     pool.  zzppooooll lliisstt can be used to check how much space the checkpoint
     takes from the pool.

